  "sport": "floorball",
  "title": "Passing in pairs",
  "description": "The players stand in pairs facing each other along the long sides, one ball per pair. Pass to your partner, who stops the ball and passes back. It takes concentration – every pass should be accurate.\n\nVariations: stop the ball with your foot before passing back, receive on the backhand and pass on the forehand (and the other way round), or pass straight back first time with control. The diagram is not to scale.",
  "coachingPoints": [
    {
      "id": "cp1",
      "text": "Pass along the floor to your partner's blade."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp2",
      "text": "Show with your stick where you want the ball."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp3",
      "text": "Soft blade when you receive – cushion the ball."
    }
  ],
